\begin{cases}
3p + e = 124 \\
5p + e = 182
\end{cases}
\] Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get $2p = 58$, so $p = 29$. Substituting $p = 29$ into the first equation, we get $3(29) + e = 124$, so $e = 17$. Therefore, the cost of a pencil is $\boxed{29}$ cents. </think> <answer> 29 </answer>

